  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability, AUC, Cmax, or permeability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "Extent of intestinal absorption and first-pass hydrolysis of the three lactone rings in humans is unknown.",
    "No formulation- or dose-specific pharmacokinetic data exist for the query.",
    "L4 solubility records are for unrelated molecules and non-physiological vehicles; no query-specific aqueous intestinal solubility or permeability data are available.",
    "Transferability of lactone-containing contexts (9-AC, clavulanic acid, ixabepilone, idarubicin) to the rigid neutral trilactone scaffold is uncertain."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) with low confidence: L1/L2 lactone-containing and polar contexts show measured oral F above 20% (9-AC ~49-50%, clavulanic acid 31.4-98.8%, ixabepilone 36.6-53%, idarubicin ~25-35%), and no affirmative sub-20% outcome transfers to this neutral non-basic trilactone. L4 solubility/dissolution records are for unrelated molecules and do not change the decision; the physicochemical low-F prior is a liability but not endpoint proof."
}

